  "application_type_full": "Full planning permission",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The unlawful House of Multiple Occupation (HMO) would result an excessive number and clustering of conversions along this section of Poynter Road, thereby unacceptably harming the character of the surrounding area, contrary to Section 5 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2021), Policies H1, H8 and H10  of the London Plan (2021), CP4 and CP5 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD5, DMD6, DMD 8, and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), the Department for Communities and Local Government Technical housing standards (2015) and the Enfield Strategic Housing Market Assessment (2015).",
    "The proposed cycle storage, by virtue of its means of access, location, no means of enclosure would fail to provide a secure, convenient and high quality facility for all types of bicycles and would fail to promote or prioritise the use of sustainable modes of transport, contrary to Section 9 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies T2, T3, T4, T5, T6, T6.1 and T7 of the London Plan (2021), CP24 and CP25 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD45, DMD46, DMD47 and DMD48 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The unauthorised development, by reason of the increased number of vehicle movements associated with the intensified use of the site, would contribute unacceptably to on street parking congestion and result in conditions prejudicial to the free flow and safety of vehicular traffic and pedestrian movements. In the absence of sufficient information demonstrating that the level of parking provision and highway impacts would be commensurate with the use proposed, the development is considered unacceptable and contrary to Section 9 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies T2, T3, T4 and T6 of the London Plan (2021), and Policies DMD45 and DMD48 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The unauthorised development, by virtue of the site constraints cannot satisfactorily accommodate all operational requirements for the HMO proposed which will intensify the use of the application property, requiring the necessary associated refuse and cycle storage capacity. This is contrary to the objectives of criterion (d) of Policy DMD5 and Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework, Policies D3, D4 and D8 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), and Policies DMD6 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its insufficient internal room sizes for the rear first floor bedroom (6.8sqm) would result in substandard and inappropriate accommodation incapable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers. The proposal is therefore contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2021), Policies D4 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD8 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
